node_modules/
dist/
*.log
.DS_Store
coverage/
outputs/
.workbuddy/

# Fixtures and demos are *inputs*, and some of them deliberately look like
# build output: a demo workspace with a `logs/` directory, a fixture whose
# report lands in `outputs/`. The rules above exclude exactly those shapes, so
# a fresh clone used to be missing files the unit suite and the demos read —
# green in a working tree that had them, red in CI. These negations restore
# them without un-ignoring the repo's own `outputs/`.
!test/fixtures/**/logs/
!test/fixtures/**/outputs/
!test/fixtures/**/*.log
!examples/**/logs/
!examples/**/*.log

# `.a2h/decisions/` is written by the viewer at runtime, not an input. Running
# the acceptance suite against `examples/radar` writes one, and committing that
# would be exactly the fabricated audit trail the protocol tells producers not
# to write. Real workspaces may still choose to commit their own.
examples/**/.a2h/decisions/
test/fixtures/**/.a2h/decisions/

# `a2h guide` output in a demo or fixture workspace. It is generated from the
# workspace's shape, so it is regenerable rather than authored: committing it
# would make every demo carry a stale copy of this repository's advice.
examples/**/.a2h/agent-guide.md
test/fixtures/**/.a2h/agent-guide.md
